From adba73720d44c622769448544da67a71ed55f0c0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John <john.de.kroon@cyberant.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 22:24:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/20] badgeui: a dump asks for a name, names can change; LF
 dumps go to Cards

- Every saved card can have a name (cards.tsv's 13th column; files
  without it read as before). Cards shows the name with the type and
  detail under it, and the type when there is none. After every dump,
  the app's own MIFARE Classic dump and any dump the client saves (the
  Console, an action), a pop-up asks for one: Enter keeps what is typed
  (empty: the type again), Esc leaves the name as it was. Rename in the
  card's options, in the list and on the card, opens it again. A name
  takes any printable character but a tab (the file's separator).
- T55xx and EM4x05 dumps (lf-t55xx-<block 1>-...-dump, lf-4x05-, -4369-,
  -4469-<UID>-dump) were lost: they now go to Cards too, on the LF card
  searched last (a T55xx dump has no UID of its own), else on a saved
  one with the ID in the name, else a new card. The dump's type becomes
  the card's. They show as 4-byte blocks; a T55xx offers Write to a
  T55xx (lf t55xx restore -f, typed in), EM4x05 nothing to write with
  (the client has no restore for it); both Edit in Write. HF > T55xx
  gains Restore.
- A card's options only offer what it can do: Simulate when the type
  has it, writing when there is a dump or none is needed.

Tested: test_pm3ui.py 22/22 on the host (new: a name after a Console
dump, Rename, Esc, an empty name; a T55xx dump alone and after an LF
search; an EM4x05 dump), screens compared by eye. Not yet on the badge.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
